						<h2><font size=3D"3" color=3D"#000000">
						<span style=3D"font-weight: 400">7. The Productivity=20
						Process</span></font></h2>
						<p><font size=3D"2">The <b>Overview</b> tab helps you see=20
						the Productivity Process behind Achieve Planner and=20
						provides easy links to the different parts of the=20
						software.</font></p>
						<p align=3D"center">
						<a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"http://www.effexis.com/achieve/screensho=
ts19/OverviewTabSS.png">
						<img border=3D"0" src=3D"http://www.effexis.com/achieve/screenshots19=
/OverviewTabSS-TN.png" width=3D"520" height=3D"419"></a><br>
						<font size=3D"1">Click Image to View Larger Size</font></p>
						<p align=3D"left"><font size=3D"2">In Step 2, you also get a=20
						notification of any new tasks (in red) that you've=20
						captured or imported in your Inbox. You can then Invoke=20
						the New Task Organizer using the link.</font></p>
						<p align=3D"left"><font size=3D"2">Using the Tools -&gt;=20
						Options menu (Display) you can set this Overview as your=20
						default 'home page' every time you start Achieve=20
						Planner.</font></p>
						<p align=3D"left"><font size=3D"2">When you
						<a href=3D"http://www.effexis.com/achieve/download.php">
						download Achieve Planner</a>, you'll get access to the=20
						Training Center, which includes a time management=20
						training course that walks you through this productivity=20
						process step-by-step.</font></p>
			<p align=3D"left">8. Project Templates</p>
			<p align=3D"left"><font size=3D"2">You can use any existing project as a=
=20
			template for creating a new project. Using templates can save you a=20
			lot of time if you have events, checklists,&nbsp; procedures, or=20
			other recurring projects that all have similar sets of tasks.</font></p>
			<p align=3D"left"><font size=3D"2">To create a new project from a=20
			template, you use the <b>File -&gt; New -&gt; New Project From Template<=
/b>=20
			menu item.</font></p>
			<p align=3D"left"><font size=3D"2">This will bring up a dialog that will=
=20
			help you select the project that you want to use as the template for=20
			the new project instance.</font></p>
			<p align=3D"center">
			<img border=3D"0" src=3D"http://www.effexis.com/achieve/screenshots19/Pr=
ojectTemplateChooser.png" width=3D"424" height=3D"352"></p>
			<p align=3D"left"><font size=3D"2">Then you can customize the new=20
			project instance as needed...</font></p>
			<p align=3D"center">
			<img border=3D"0" src=3D"http://www.effexis.com/achieve/screenshots19/Ne=
wTemplateProjectDetails.png" width=3D"520" height=3D"207"></p>
			<p align=3D"left"><font size=3D"2">before adding it to the outline.</fon=
t></p>
			<p align=3D"left"><font size=3D"2">Some tips for getting the most from=
=20
			project templates:</font></p>
			<ul>
				<li>
				<p align=3D"left"><font size=3D"2">I recommend creating a special=20
				'Templates' project to store/organize all your templates</font></p></li=
>
			<li>
			<p align=3D"left"><font size=3D"2">Add a prefix to all your template=20
			projects (like 'TP-') to make them easier to find using the template=20
			chooser dialog filter.</font></p></li>
		<li>
		<p align=3D"left"><font size=3D"2">Set the priority of template projects =
to=20
		D to hide them in the Task Chooser</font></p></li>
	</ul>
						<p align=3D"left">9. Life Planning System</p>
						<p align=3D"left"><font size=3D"2">Achieve Planner is more=20
						than just a productivity tool, it is a comprehensive=20
						life planning system. In the end, being more productive=20
						doesn't matter unless you are heading in the right=20
						direction and creating the kinds of results that you=20
						really want in your life.</font></p>
						<div align=3D"center">
				<table border=3D"1" width=3D"490" cellspacing=3D"0" cellpadding=3D"2" i=
d=3D"table4" class=3D"testimonial">
					<tbody><tr>
						<td>
						<p style=3D"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0">
						<font size=3D"2">"<b>The best life=20
						planner I've ever used!</b> When it comes to=20
						doing complete "Life Planning" there are=20
