PerformanceMainPageTN.png" width=3D"300" height=3D"249" alt=3D"View your pr=
ogress using metrics" align=3D"right" hspace=3D"10"></a>Each=20
						goal contains an entry where you can record individual=20
						achievement/progress milestones.</font></p><p align=3D"left">
						<font size=3D"2">In addition, you can track measurable=20
						values using <b>metrics</b>, which allow you to enter=20
						numeric values for any measurements you want to track.</font></p><p a=
lign=3D"left">
						<font size=3D"2">Use performance reports to view your=20
						progress in each metric you are tracking.</font></p><h2><font size=3D=
"3" color=3D"#000000">
						<span style=3D"font-weight: 400">10</span></font><font color=3D"#0000=
00"><span style=3D"font-weight: 400"><font size=3D"3">.=20
						Two-Way Sync With Microsoft=20
						Outlook</font><font size=3D"3" face=3D"Times New Roman">=AE</font></s=
pan></font></h2>
						<p><font size=3D"2">If you use Microsoft Outlook<font face=3D"Times N=
ew Roman">=AE</font>=20
						(XP/2003/2007), Achieve Planner can keep your=20
						appointments and tasks synchronized with your Outlook=20
						calendar and tasks folders.</font></p>
						<p><font size=3D"2">Since Outlook synchronizes to most=20
						PDAs, Smartphone and Blackberries, you can use it to=20
						synchronize your data and take it with you.</font></p>
						<p><font size=3D"2">You can even track action-oriented emails as=20
						projects/tasks in Achieve Planner.</font></p>
	<p><font size=3D"2">There are two ways to do this:</font></p>
	<p><font size=3D"2"><b>Import Emails Directly</b></font></p>
	<p><font size=3D"2">In the Outlook Synchronization Settings (use Tools -&g=
t;=20
	Outlook Synchronization then click Settings button), you'll find a Hot Key=
 (Alt+Win+E=20
	by default) to import the currently selected email(s) from Outlook into=20
	Achieve Planner.</font></p>
	<p align=3D"center">
	<img border=3D"0" src=3D"http://www.effexis.com/achieve/screenshots19/Impo=
rtEmailHotkey.png" width=3D"527" height=3D"238"></p>
						<p><font size=3D"2"><b>Import Emails Automatically</b></font></p>
	<p><font size=3D"2">The other option is to create a special folder in Outl=
ook=20
	(like 'Todo' under your Inbox) and tell Achieve Planner to import new emai=
ls=20
	from this folder as tasks during the next Outlook Synchronization.</font><=
/p>
						<p><font size=3D"2"><b>NOTE:</b> In order to import emails=20
						from Outlook, you must set the Outlook settings to=20
						Import Email AND select the folder(s) from which you want=20
						to import emails.</font></p>
	<p><font size=3D"2">Imported emails are collected under the <b>Inbox</b>=
=20
	special project for later processing.</font></p>
	<p><font size=3D"2"><b>Other Outlook Synchronization Options</b></font></p=
>
						<p><font size=3D"2">Achieve Planner can also synchronize=20
						your Outlook tasks, appointments and contacts.</font></p>
	<p><font size=3D"2">By default, Achieve Planner only imports data from=20
	Outlook, but you can change the settings to perform a full 2-way sync.</fo=
nt></p>
						<h2><font size=3D"3" color=3D"#000000">
